            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I totally missed 'JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring' (probably because by the name and common examples I thought that it is mostly about Typescript :) ). \r\nSo, @SuperCuber, it *kind of* works with 'mini.comment': it updates `commentstring` option on every `CursorHold` event (triggered after cursor is idle for `updatetime` milliseconds). So it is like: position cursor, wait for `updatetime` milliseconds, comment with \"appropriate\" comment structure.\r\n\r\nFor full support, 'mini.comment' needs to implement \"pre-comment\" hook. Which I am more inclined to add, than multi-language support.",
